e 2024 Summer Olympics took place on August 2 and 3, at the Châteauroux Shooting Centre in France, featuring 30 competitors from 25 nations."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the qualification round, " [:a {:href "/athletes/154239"} "Conner Prince"] " led with a score of 124 out of 125, advancing to the final alongside " [:a {:href "/athletes/144197"} "Tammaro Cassandro"] " of Italy, " [:a {:href "/athletes/154227"} "Lee Meng-Yuan"] " (TPE), " [:a {:href "/athletes/117326"} "Vincent Hancock"] " (USA), " [:a {:href "/athletes/121140"} "Stefan Nilsson"] " of Sweden, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/124744"} "Nicolás Pacheco"] " of Peru."] "\n\n" [:p {} "American shooter Vincent Hancock secured the gold medal, marking his fourth Olympic gold in men’s skeet. His teammate and prodigy, Conner Prince, earned the silver medal, while Lee Meng-Yuan of Chinese Taipei took bronze. The final was competitive, with Hancock ultimately clinching the gold when Prince missed one of the final series of birds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Hancock’s victory solidified his position as one of the most successful shooters in Olympic history, with a unique record of having won and retained his title twice with the interruption of a failure at the 2016 Olympics. Prince’s silver highlighted the overall strength of the U.S. shooting team, particularly in this event."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Qualifying Shoot-Off 1-3"] [:th {} "Qualifying Shoot-Off 5-9"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1950"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117326"} "Vincent Hancock"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "123 (4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "58 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:cla